@1401 = ~Vridomir...... I sense Vridomir...~
@1402 = ~This staff? Is this what you want, spirit? *Showing the staff to the revenant*~
@1403 = ~Die, foul creature!~
@1404 = ~Vridomir the cursed... Vridomir the killer.... He is with you.~
@1405 = ~I am not a friend of Vridomir. I merely carry his imprisoned soul.~~I am not a friend of Vridomir. I merely carry his imprisoned soul.~
@1406 = ~What connection do you have with Vridomir, spirit? Explain yourself....~
@1407 = ~Why should I give this staff to a rotting undead creature?~
@1408 = ~Vridomir killed me..... along with many others, in a single night. I am the vengeance of all those who fell. We want Vridomir's end.~
@1409 = ~Would having this staff bring you peace? Very well, it is yours.~
@14010 = ~Fine. But I paid dearly to obtain this staff. Do you have anything else to give me in exchange?~
@14011 = ~I see. But you will not have my staff. You are nothing but another monster. Begone.~
@14012 = ~Thank you.~
@14013 = ~*The revenant breaks the staff in two. Vridomir's soul floats in the air for a few moments before the revenant grabs it and crushes it between his hands. Then he turns to dust.*~
@14014 = ~I still possess enough power: I can grant you all of Vridomir's powers. It is the least I can offer; I should not even have to do this.~
@14015 = ~All of his powers? Wow. I accept. Do your duty, avenger.~
@14016 = ~Hmmf. It seems too good to be true. Something smells like a trick. No. The only thing you will receive is your death, foul monster.~
@14017 = ~*The revenant breaks the staff in two. Vridomir's soul floats in the air for a few moments before the revenant grabs it and crushes it between his hands. You feel an immense new power awakening within you. Then the undead creature turns to dust.*~